   },
   "text": "Signal Attenuation Through a Lossy Cable: Fitting the Decay Model"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i1",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.452,
    "y": 0.22284,
    "w": 0.09599,
    "h": 0.01509
   },
   "text": "D. Measure"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i2",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.44393,
    "y": 0.25372,
    "w": 0.11215,
    "h": 0.01509
   },
   "text": "October 2026"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i3",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.46419,
    "y": 0.3066,
    "w": 0.07163,
    "h": 0.01258
   },
   "text": "Abstract"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i4",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.17398,
    "y": 0.3305,
    "w": 0.65205,
    "h": 0.04277
   },
   "text": "A tone is injected into a lossy cable and the received amplitude is recorded against distance. We fit the measured data to the two-parameter decay model and report the residual of the fit."
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i5",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.39965,
    "w": 0.16036,
    "h": 0.01811
   },
   "text": "1 The model"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i6",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.43391,
    "w": 0.44973,
    "h": 0.01377
   },
   "text": "The received amplitude follows the exponential decay law"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i7",
   "kind": "formula",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.45796,
    "y": 0.46339,
    "w": 0.41262,
    "h": 0.01523
   },
   "latex": "y = a \\, e ^ { - b x } ,"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i8",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.4958,
    "w": 0.74118,
    "h": 0.03088
   },
   "text": "where x is distance in metres, y the measured amplitude, a the launch amplitude and b the attenuation constant."
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i9",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.55283,
    "w": 0.203,
    "h": 0.01811
   },
   "text": "2 Measurements"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i10",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.58709,
    "w": 0.27897,
    "h": 0.01377
   },
   "text": "The bench data used for the fit are:"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i11",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.73357,
    "w": 0.15917,
    "h": 0.01811
   },
   "text": "3 Fit quality"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i12",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.76783,
    "w": 0.74118,
    "h": 0.03088
   },
   "text": "The least-squares fit of the model to the measured data above is assessed by its residual pattern; a systematic residual indicates a non-exponential loss channel."
  },
